ble-data, old-muon here. (2) THE LADDER RUNS THE WRONG WAY, AND THE TABLE SHOWS IT. Going from N=0 to N=1 moves the prediction AWAY from CODATA: +1.31 keV (1677.5 ppm) becomes +9.01 keV (11511 ppm), a 6.9x REGRESSION -- because the N=1 term multiplies E_0 by (1 + hbar_q^2), which can only increase an already-high value. That is 118x the table's own '97.3 ppm ceiling' (which I confirm computes to 97.333 ppm). And it flatly contradicts prf:q-beta-spectral-bridge, which asserts 'At $N \\geq 1$, the bound is sub-keV' and 'Finite-depth truncations recover the exact Q_beta exponentially fast in depth N'. The chapter's own N=1 number refutes the chapter's own convergence claim. GOOD PRACTICE NOTED: the .ts authorNote says the parent block prop:q-beta-form-a-n1-symbolic does not exist and that uses[] was dropped rather than re-pointed -- VERIFIED, no block in content/ carries that label.","history":1},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","severity":"major","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:p02","notes":"No block-final sentence restating what the text already established.","history":1},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:p02","notes":"No reflex three-item list; enumerations present are driven by the underlying content.","history":1},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","notes":"block has no .lean sibling","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stal